Z||000010||lowCG||07-27-2000||10:58 AM||||What gear did you assign?<BR>Not quite sure of the differences between the '95,and '97 ECM(what I have),but Terry has convinced me that the most versatile solution to complete control is an early ECM,and some carefull re-programming.<BR>Of course I like the idea of using what I have,so I'm trying to sort it out the best I can before making any changes to the ECM;it's close,but something is just not quite right,and I am willing to live without perfection if I can get some things right,maybe sensors,which I'll be replacing soon,just to see if there's a difference.<BR>So what did you do for an exhaust on your car?<BR>Did you use a "dogbone" in mounting your engine?<BR>Did you do anything for the #2 02 sensor?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||filthyscarecrow||07-28-2000||12:47 AM||||after my little "on track excursion," (who have i whipped...) i decided i needed more power, just so i could keep up with the vipers... i was considering a turbo, but if the 3400 is an easy swap i might do that. i'm pretty good at fabricating parts and wiring things into the system. how much trouble should i expect? how much did you spend on the engine? i am thinking i would swap my 4 spd for a 5 spd as well... input would be appreciated, thanks...<P>------------------<BR>me go fast.||||reg||1
